# QuantumShield — Supabase-Only Architecture

## Stack (do NOT introduce MongoDB, self-hosted Postgres, or 12 Docker microservices)

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| Frontend | `web/` — Next.js 15 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Framer Motion, Recharts, Zustand |
| API | Next.js Route Handlers under `web/src/app/api/` (single gateway, not separate Express services) |
| Database | **Supabase PostgreSQL** via Prisma (`web/prisma/schema.prisma`) |
| Auth | NextAuth v5 + Prisma adapter; demo user via `web/src/lib/demo-auth.ts` |
| Real-time | Supabase Realtime + SSE for scan progress (`web/src/lib/scan-engine.ts`) |
| Background jobs | Database-backed queue tables + Vercel cron OR Python worker (`core/`, `scanner.py`) |
| File storage | Supabase Storage (reports, evidence, screenshots) |
| Deploy | Vercel (`web/`), Root Directory = `web` |

**Connection strings:**
- `DATABASE_URL` → Supabase **transaction pooler** port **6543** (`?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1`)
- `DIRECT_URL` → direct port **5432** (migrations/seed only)

