## Logs & events (replace MongoDB)

Use Postgres tables with `Json` columns:

```prisma
model ScanLog {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  scanId    String
  phase     String
  message   String
  metadata  Json?
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  @@index([scanId])
}

model AgentLog {
  id          String   @id @default(cuid())
  agentId     String
  executionId String?
  level       String
  message     String   @db.Text
  metadata    Json?
  createdAt   DateTime @default(now())
  @@index([agentId])
}

model HealthCheck {
  id           String   @id @default(cuid())
  serviceName  String
  status       String
  responseMs   Int?
  details      Json?
  createdAt    DateTime @default(now())
  @@index([serviceName, createdAt])
}
```

Publish scan/agent updates via Supabase Realtime on `scan:{id}` and `agent:{id}` channels.

## Implementation phases (strict order)

1. **Foundation** — Prisma schema, auth, org RBAC, sidebar shell (`web/src/components/layout/`)
2. **Deep Scanner** — Real DNS/HTTP/SSL/path checks; store findings; SSE progress; no fake progress bars
3. **Agents** — CRUD + scheduled runs (cron) + log streaming; monitor template must hit real URLs
4. **Module APIs** — API security, cloud, phishing, compliance — each reads/writes Supabase via Prisma
5. **System health** — `/api/health` + periodic checks persisted to `HealthCheck`
6. **Polish** — Reports export, academy content, performance

## Scanner requirements (must be real)

When user runs a scan on a verified domain:

1. DNS resolve + subdomain wordlist probe (`core/subdomain_enum.py` or TS equivalent)
2. TCP connect on common ports (80, 443, 8080, 3000, 22)
3. HTTP fetch — security headers (HSTS, CSP, X-Frame-Options)
4. TLS cert expiry and cipher check
5. Path fuzz (`/admin`, `/api`, `/.env`, `/backup`)
6. Persist `Finding` rows with severity, CWE, remediation
7. Stream phase progress to client

Scan modes: LIGHTNING (fast subset), STANDARD (13 phases), MEGA (extended fuzz), SUPER (alternate engine in `core/`).

## Agent requirements (must be real)

- `Agent` model: type `monitor|responder|hunter|compliance`, `cronSchedule`, `config` Json
- On run: execute typed handler (not empty mock); append `AgentLog` rows
- Monitor agent: HTTP GET + SSL days-left check every N minutes
- Surface logs in terminal UI (`dashboard/agent-security`)

## API conventions

- All routes under `web/src/app/api/` require session or API key
- Validate with Zod; return `{ error, code }` JSON on failure
- Org-scoped queries: always filter by `orgId` from session
- Rate limit sensitive routes in middleware

## Env vars (Supabase + Vercel)

Required: `DATABASE_URL`, `DIRECT_URL`, `AUTH_SECRET`, `AUTH_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL`

See `DEPLOY.md` and `web/.env.example`. Never commit `.env` or `VERCEL_ENV.txt`.

